This is wrong because: (1) a client-only app has no database or secrets; (2) 'yourSecretKeyHere'/'yourApiKeyHere' are placeholder values — generated code must never contain placeholders; (3) hardcoded secrets are a security defect.

Rules:
  1. Client-only apps: config holds ONLY game/UI constants — never DATABASE_URL, SECRET_KEY, API_KEY, API_PREFIX, process.env.
  2. No placeholder values ('your...Here', '...example', empty strings used as real config).
